  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Shelter and Non Food Items Assistance to Displaced Persons due to Floods in N&apos;Djamena and the Lac</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Over the past few weeks, the height of the Chari River in Chad has increased from less than 7m to more than 8m and continues to rise, causing immense flooding along its banks. Currently, N&apos;Djamena has more than 98,785 people displaced due to flooding. As the river continues to rise, displacement is expected to continue in the N&apos;Djamena area. In addition, downstream of the river is the Lac province, which is expected to suffer a considerable impact from the rise of the Chari River in the coming weeks. In order to respond to the floods in N&apos;djamena and the Lac Province, IOM is providing lifesaving assistance, including emergency shelter and essential non-food item kits.</narrative>
  </description>
